  "claim": "The man who released the 1994 platinum selling album, Nineteen Ninety-Four, and another singer were both lead vocalists for bands. Miracle (Nonpoint song) featured this other singer.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Alvin Lee. Sentence: Alvin Lee (born Graham Anthony Barnes; 19 December 1944 – 6 March 2013) was an English singer and guitarist, best known as the lead vocalist and lead guitarist of the blues rock band Ten Years After.\nPage: Chad Gray. Sentence: Chad Gray (born October 16, 1971), is the lead vocalist for the groove metal supergroup Hellyeah and former lead vocalist for American heavy metal band Mudvayne.\nPage: Nineteen Ninety-Four (album). Sentence: Nineteen Ninety-Four (Viceroy VIC 8012-2, Reissue: Repertoire REP5191) is a 1994 album by Alvin Lee released in the United States as I Hear You Rockin'\nPage: Miracle (Nonpoint song). Sentence: It features Chad Gray of Mudvayne fame contributing vocals during the song's chorus.",
