        "original_id": "b0e2c302-56ec-518e-8745-49e1c26b243c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alvin Lee, Chad Gray\n- Bands: Ten Years After, Hellyeah, Mudvayne\n- Works: Nineteen Ninety-Four, I Hear You Rockin', Miracle\n\nFacts:\n- Alvin Lee, born Graham Anthony Barnes on 19 December 1944 and died on 6 March 2013, was an English singer and guitarist.\n- Alvin Lee was best known as the lead vocalist and lead guitarist of the blues rock band Ten Years After.\n- Nineteen Ninety-Four is a 1994 album by Alvin Lee.\n- Nineteen Ninety-Four was released in the United States as I Hear You Rockin'.\n- Chad Gray was born on October 16, 1971.\n- Chad Gray is the lead vocalist for the groove metal supergroup Hellyeah.\n- Chad Gray was the former lead vocalist for the American heavy metal band Mudvayne.\n- The song Miracle features Chad Gray, known from Mudvayne, contributing vocals during the chorus.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
